Interactive USD edits of implicit shapes and of a native arnold prim, with the usd procedural and the render delegate

A sphere, a cube, a cylinder, a cone, a capsule and an ArnoldSphere have their radius, size, axis or height edited,
the stage being re-rendered after each edit.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural (hydra reader) reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive
render session, and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues
in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
